E29 is definitive: all 103 pending messages are `process_invoice` kind, oldest created at t=457, with up to 37 attempts. There are no other message kinds stuck. The entire queue backup and throughput drop is explained by a single cause: invoice layout changed at ~t=457, causing extraction failures, a retry storm, and queue saturation. The sync-job deploy (E12) is a decoy — E27 shows no connection issues and sync-job has no dependents (E24); the ledger slowdown (E4) is a downstream symptom of fewer invoices completing.

